ia for Afghan refugees.</article-title><source>Trans R Soc Trop Med Hyg</source><volume>90</volume><fpage>357</fpage><lpage>361</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8882175</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000101-Lindsay1"><label>39</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lindsay</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Snow</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Armstrong</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Greenwood</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>Permethrin-impregnated bednets reduce nuisance arthropods in Gambian houses.</article-title><source>Med Vet Entomol</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>377</fpage><lpage>383</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2519687</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000101-Temu1"><label>40</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Temu</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Minjas</surname><given-names>JN</given-names></name><name><surname>Shiff</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Majala</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Bedbug control by permethrin-impregnated bednets in Tanzania.</article-title><source>Med Vet Entomol</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>457</fpage><lpage>459</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10608237</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>